Title: Custom Website Enhancements Plugin

Description: This WordPress plugin enhances an existing website by adding custom post type, widget, and shortcodes that are stylistically consistent with the website's branding and design.

Prerequisites:

1. A PHP development environment (e.g., XAMPP, WAMP, MAMP).
2. WordPress installed locally or remotely (e.g., WordPress.com, WordPress.org).
3. Familiarity with WordPress theme development and plugin development.

Features:

1. Custom Post Type: "Services" (singular: Service) enabling users to create, manage, and display various services offered by the website.

    - Required fields: Title, Description
    - Optional fields: Featured image, Categories, Tags, Custom fields (e.g., Pricing, Duration)

2. New Widget: "Services List" displaying a list of services sorted by alphabetical order.

    - Widget options: Number of services to display, Custom ordering (e.g., By popularit, By price)

3. Additional Shortcodes:

   - [Services_List limit="5" orderby="price" order="asc"]
   - Displays a list of the five latest services sorted by ascending price.

   - [Service content="excerpt" cat_slug="design"]
   - Displays a Service post excerpt if its category slug is 'design'.

   - [Service_Image service_id="123"]
   - Displays the Featured Image of a Service post with the ID 123.

4. Styles: This plugin adheres to the existing website's color scheme, font stack, and other design elements.

   - Identical colour palette, typography, and other visual properties to the website.

   - Custom CSS added to avoid styling conflicts with the child theme.

Compatibility: Compatible with the latest version of WordPress (as of this writing, version 5.8.3)

Installation:

1. Download the plugin file, "custom-website-enhancements.zip," from the repository.
2. Navigate to the WordPress admin dashboard > Plugins > Add New.
3. Upload the downloaded ZIP file and click "Install Now."
4. Once installed, click "Activate" to activate the plugin.

Plugin Description:

This WordPress plugin, "Custom Website Enhancements," improves an existing WordPress website by adding a customizable Services post type, a Services List widget, and enhanced shortcodes.

Plugin Settings:

1. Services Custom Post Type:
   - Go to Settings > Custom Website Enhancements.
   - Configure custom post type fields and default values (optional).

2. Services List Widget:
   - Go to Appearance > Widgets.
   - Drag-and-drop the Services List widget into a widget area of your choice.
   - Configure widget options as needed.

3. Shortcodes:
   - The shortcodes can be added to the editor or through a template file (recommended).
   - For example, add [Services_List limit="5" orderby="price" order="asc"] shortcode in a page, post, or widget.

Code Documentation:

The plugin's code follows the latest WordPress coding standards, with detailed comments explaining critical sections and variables.

1. Plugin details: The plugin header defines the plugin information and dependencies.

   ```
